        "text": "The answer depends on how the clause is worded and on the parties’ true intention. Under the principle of freedom, voluntariness of commitment and agreement (Article 3 of the Civil Code 2015), the parties are free to design how the contract is terminated and liquidated. Three common wordings lead to three different outcomes: [1]"
